    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1129">

                <pb facs="0936" n="926" sameAs="frus:frus1949v08/pg926"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">125.3513/10–449: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State
                        to the Consul at Dairen</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Paddock</hi>)<anchor n="79" xml:id="d1129-f1"/>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1949-10-04T14:00:00-05:00">October 4, 1949—2
                            p. m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>166. If evac ship plans reported to you in recent tels materialize and if Chaos
                    unable leave aboard such ship, Dept reluctantly of opinion your [and]
                    Gleysteen’s departure shld not be delayed if exit permits Chaos not forthcoming.
                    Publicity only lever which might be effective this situation, but Dept of
                    opinion such pressure wld not result in favorable action re either Chao, wld
                    probably have undesirable effect further jeopardizing your departure and
                    possibly make more difficult position Chaos if they have to remain Dairen.
                    Pressure through SCAP believed impossible.</p>
                <pb facs="0937" n="927" xml:id="pg927"/>
                <p>When time comes to leave you shld therefore make payments Shou-yu and family
                    Yi-hsien accordance instructions separate tels.</p>
                <p>As for official documents, you already authorized destroy all classified
                    material. This shld leave only accts which may be examined provided (1) exam
                    cannot be avoided and your departure wld otherwise be impossible (2) you destroy
                    or render innocuous all compromising material.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Webb</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d1129-f1" n="79" type="source" xml:id="d1129-f1-content">
                <p>Repeated to the Ambassador in the Soviet Union as telegram No. 729.</p>
            </note>
